  "worked_solution": "First, we complete the squares for the variable ${x}_{1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}^{2} & =\\frac{35}{3} \\\\ 3({x}_{1}^{2}-\\frac{2}{3}{x}_{1})+4{x}_{2}^{2} & =\\frac{35}{3} \\\\ 3({x}_{1}^{2}-\\frac{2}{3}{x}_{1}+{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{2}-{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{2})+4{x}_{2}^{2} & =\\frac{35}{3} \\\\ 3{({x}_{1}-\\frac{1}{3})}^{2}-3{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{2}+4{x}_{2}^{2} & =\\frac{35}{3} \\\\ 3{({x}_{1}-\\frac{1}{3})}^{2}-\\frac{1}{3}+4{x}_{2}^{2} & =\\frac{35}{3} \\\\ 3{({x}_{1}-\\frac{1}{3})}^{2}+4{x}_{2}^{2} & =\\frac{36}{3} \\\\ 3{({x}_{1}-\\frac{1}{3})}^{2}+4{x}_{2}^{2} & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, performing the change of variables\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}={x}_{1}-\\frac{1}{3}, \\\\ {y}_{2}={x}_{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{y}_{1}^{2}+4{y}_{2}^{2} & =12 \\\\ \\frac{{y}_{1}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}_{2}^{2}}{3} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{y}_{1}^{2}}{{2}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}_{2}^{2}}{(\\sqrt{3})^{2}} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThis represents an ellipse with semiaxes $2$ and $\\sqrt{3}.$",
